  "reading_limit": "this measures TRACEABILITY, not semantic digestion: a clause may already be fully expanded in a PLAN file by an author who wrote neither the V-id nor the section anchor, and that counts as unmapped (the correct action is to register or expand, not to declare failure). Conversely a section-anchor hit does NOT prove the clause was expanded, because one VISION section can carry several clauses. Worse, the anchor string is AMBIGUOUS ACROSS DOCUMENTS: `S5.1` inside 07_MINI_MODEL_DELIVERY is that doc's own CAP-0 section, not VISION 5.1, so section_citations is an upper bound and any claim built on it must name the citing sentence (measured 2026-10-11: the seven unmapped clauses' anchors hit 1-8 other docs, several of them false). Counts are taken over the PLAN files attributed to that clause's N-code only, so a clause discussed in another line's file is not credited here."
